<title>BELGIUM: EU experts postpone vote on U.S. grain quota.</title>
<headline>EU experts postpone vote on U.S. grain quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's (EU) rice management committee on Thursday postponed a vote on details of export certificates needed for the import of U.S. rice under GATT quota arrangements, an EU official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The vote was delayed because of pressure of other business,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The quota arrangement will allow the U.S. to export to the EU 38,721 tonnes of milled and semi-milled rice, 7,642 tonnes of husked rice and 5,461 tonnes of broken rice.</p>
<p>If adopted the quota will be open for bids five days after the regulation comes into force which will be three days after publication in the EU Official Journal. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
